<title>USA: Century says may sell Australian stake.</title>
<headline>Century says may sell Australian stake.</headline>
<dateline>NEW CANAAN, Conn. 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Century Communications Corp said Tuesday it is in discussions with investment advisers to sell its stake in its Australian operations.</p>
<p>Century said it has not yet come up with an estimate of the net proceeds to be derived from such a sale. It also said it has not come up with an expected period required for completion of such a transaction.</p>
<p>Century owns and operates cable television systems, radio stations, and, through a subsidiary, cellular telephone systems.</p>
